# Stock bootloader identity (Phase 8a fix round, finding 9): the sha256 of
# build/boot/bootloader.bin built with the version string pinned, so the
# bytes do not depend on the commit or the date. validate.sh builds
# build/boot with the same VERSION and fails when the hash differs.
# Recorded from main ab6df75672 with arm-none-eabi-gcc 16.2.0
# (04f555b9e88f1b80...). Re-recorded at p090-int5s (2026-11-14), same
# compiler, for one deliberate fix in a file the stock bootloader links:
#   disk_cache.o  p090-fsfix #355 (ledger 2.109): a buffer's slot from its
#                 byte offset; .text 53,128 both, the index code changed
# (firmware/core_alloc.c also changed in int5s, simulator-only code.)
# Re-record only when a deliberate change reaches the stock bootloader:
#   git archive <ref> | tar -x -C <tmp> && cd <tmp> && mkdir -p build/boot &&
#   cd build/boot && ../../tools/configure --target=22 --type=b \
#       --compiler-prefix=arm-none-eabi- </dev/null &&
#   make VERSION=ipodui-boot-identity && shasum -a 256 bootloader.bin
9935d934981043732e34724b824c918dc9753528562ea61352fea7847ed84d1e  bootloader.bin
